/target
.DS_Store

# Python bytecode. Nothing here is built from Python, but the committed
# evidence tree carries scripts that get run, and the compiled output of a
# run is not evidence. The `.pyc` already tracked under
# `reference/sergeant-upstream/` deliberately stays tracked (R-S0-8):
# `reference/UPSTREAM.md` pins that tree byte-for-byte to an upstream SHA, so
# untracking it would break a provenance claim to tidy up a file the language
# bar never counted. This rule is about the next one, not that one.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.sergeant/data
repos/
.sergeant.toml.lock
sergeant.toml.validate-*
